autoterm (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Commands that can run other commands (env, fd, rg) and history are
    no longer corrected silently; they ask first like everything else.
  * fish: abbreviations are no longer suggested. fish can't run one by
    name, so accepting it failed and taught a fix that never works.
  * Suggestions nobody answered aren't logged, so a password typed at
    the prompt by mistake doesn't reach the disk.
  * New autoterm reset: the way out when the log fails its checksum,
    which an interrupted write could cause, after which nothing could
    be recorded again.

 -- Thallium Project <36neelansh@gmail.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 03:33:20 +0530

autoterm (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: typo correction for unknown commands in fish and
    bash, with confirm-before-run for anything not read-only, learning
    from overrides and a checksummed audit log.

 -- Thallium Project <36neelansh@gmail.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 03:28:22 +0530
